    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "rqTu2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -380,
      "name": "Token provenance",
      "width": 520,
      "height": 280,
      "content": "walkie · Broomva foundation, native mobile adapter\n\nPencil stores color as hex; Broomva's canonical source is OKLCH. Converted once, documented here, never re-eyeballed.\n\nink #0C101A = oklch(0.175 0.022 265)\npaper #FFFFFF = oklch(1 0 0)\ncanvas-soft #F3F4F6 = oklch(0.966 0.003 265)\ncanvas-deep #060810 = oklch(0.135 0.020 272)\nice #F2F3F6 = oklch(0.965 0.004 265)\nblue #5480C7 = oklch(0.60 0.12 260)\ntidepool #009BD8 = oklch(0.65 0.14 235)\nslate #3D424D = oklch(0.38 0.020 265)\nmuted #5F636C = oklch(0.50 0.015 265)\ngreen #00A24F = oklch(0.62 0.17 152)\namber #DCA81C = oklch(0.76 0.15 85)\nred #D42325 = oklch(0.56 0.21 27)\n\nAdapter decision: blue-text light = #436EB4 = oklch(0.54 0.12 260).\nResonant AI Blue is 3.97:1 on paper, below the 4.5:1 text floor. It is kept\nunchanged for icons and fills (non-text needs 3:1) and darkened on the same\nhue axis only where it carries text. Dark theme keeps #5480C7 throughout.\n\nWork states are the design system's canonical six: Queued, Running, Stuck,\nNeeds you, Done, Standing. Needs you is a filled tidepool chip, Running is a\ntidepool dot; structure separates them so colour never carries meaning alone."
    }
  ],
